Z||000045||batboy||11-11-2000||10:43 AM||||I've been trying hard to stay out of this debate. But, I've noticed that numerous forum members, ones I thought had some common sense and intellegence, are calling the poor voters that got confused, morons and worse. I hope when you guys get elderly and are trying to peer down through your bifocals at a tiny printed ballot and can't quite figure it out immediately, that someone calls you a moron too. Have a little compassion, these people might be our grandparents and are real people with real rights too.<P>All you Bush supporters...back off. There is no winner yet because all the ballots have not been counted. Those absentee ballets could make a big difference to the outcome. At least in Palm Beach County, there is a good case that the ballot might be illegal according to Florida law.<P>Doesn't it seem strange that G.W. Bush's brother is govenor in a state where there is documented election irregualities. Ballot boxes missing, minorities turned away, sample ballots published before the elections were not the same as used, etc, etc.<P>Combine this with the fact that Gore appears to have the majority of the popular vote. Sounds like the America people want Gore for president to me. Any proven voter fraud and election tampering should be resolved quickly and harshly. It's very important that this should never happen again.<P>The Republican party in general has been paying off major kickbacks and playing dirty for years now. It's time to say we've had enough and put a stop to this bullschitt. Bush ought to keep his big mouth shut until the election count is officially verified and is completed. Any possible illegal activity should be solved in court. That is the American way.||||reg||1
Z||000046||deceler8||11-11-2000||12:53 PM||||If anything, Jeb Bush has distinguished himself by recusing himself from the process. <P>And the election process is basically handled by the Dems in Florida...after all, the state Atty. General is a Democrat...<P>I also agree that both candidates should shut the fugg up...if they both want to move forward with appointments as if they expect to be elected that is fine with me. Some may call that showboating, but I believe it demonstrates to the world that there will be a continuity of leadership regardless of what happens.<P>I am appalled at the practice of rounding up nursing home residents and homeless folks and people of questionable citizenship to vote in any election...if they don't understand the issues and the voting process, for whatever reason, they should be excluded from the process. Remember, a lot of perfectly healthy, informed voters didn't even bother to take the time.<P>There are twice as many registered Democrats in Florida than Republicans...the real issue to Gore and the Democrats should be why they didn't show up to vote for their guy. <P>Tennessee would have clinched it for Gore had he won his home state.||||reg||1
Z||000047||theogre||11-11-2000||01:12 PM||||On the cadidates... Doesn't matter who gets in. They are both pathetic.<P>On the problematic Florida Ballot... I do allot of readability and functional type testing of print and manufacturing stuff. That ballot is a horrible design. Ignore the numerous drawings and look at actual photos showing the whole ballot and the way it lays in the real world. (CNN has one of the better photos.)<P>You have an alignment issue right off the bat. Not only must the card be perfectly placed in the punch bed, but the printing on the wing pages must also be perfectly placed and those pages must be inserted into the machine perfectly as well. There's at least 3 potential falures right there.<P>Add to this that many people are vision impared. The mispunch number goes up fast.<P>For those of you that don't understand how the ballot works, go to K/wall mart etc and look at the poster display stand in the toy department. Imagine the posters are the white ballot sheets with all the names and you have to punch a hole in a card in between the poster frames. You finish that column and turn the frame to expose the next voting column on the punch card. Any slack in the frames, misalignment of the ballot sheets, or misalignment of the punch card, and you have the kind of problem holding up florida. <P>The problem here is that the Florida board of elections is grossly incompetant or corrupt. Their own testing should have exposed this problem years ago. The odds they don't know of the problems I described above are very small. There is no excuse for this ballot design to exist. This isn't the first time this ballot design has shown these problems.||||reg||1
Z||000048||2M4 Dale||11-11-2000||02:20 PM||||Jeb Bush has nothing to do with the election process in Florida.......to try to blame him for missing ballot boxes etc. is inane.<P>There are election irregularities in every state....every time. And the only one I hear screaming discrimination is Jesse Jackson....so whats new ?<P>If anyone had any problems with the ballot then they should have asked for help. I would have....I wear bi-focals !<P>The ballot was preapproved by both parties and designed with seniors in mind by a Democrat.<P>To say the the Replublicans have been underwriting dirty deals and payoffs and not saying that the Democrats do the same is assinine.<P>The electoral college elects the president...thats a Constitutional FACT !!! The popular vote does not...and thats a FACT !!!Be it right or wrong we can't change the rules in the middle of the game. Both candidates were and are aware of the rules.<P><BR>HOW MANY RECOUNTS WILL THE DEMOCRATS REQUIRE ???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000049||My7Fieros||11-11-2000||03:20 PM||||THIS IS GETTING UGLY. <BR>ANY OF YOU WHO CAN ACTUALLY SAY THAT BALLET WAS CONFUSING ARE OBVIOUSLY <B>MORONS!!!</B><BR>WHAT A SORRY ASS EXCUSE!!!! MY GOD, THIS IS A BAD OMEN FOR THE FUTURE OF OUR COUNTRY.<BR>BOO HOO...I DONT LIKE THE OUTCOME..LETS JUST KEEP COUNTING AND SAY THE HELL WITH THE LAWS..I WANT MY PERSON TO WIN.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000050||batboy||11-11-2000||03:35 PM||||Easy now Dale, don't get your undies in a bunch. Florida State law required the statewide recount, not the Democrats. Regardless of what anyone thinks, the election process is not over until all the votes are counted, verified, certified, and made official. That includes all absentee ballots too.<P>I said the majority of the American people want Gore for president, which is quite true, just look at the popular vote. There have been 2 or 3 U.S. presidents in history that did not get the popular vote, but were elected. Yes, this is quite possible and legal, assuming the election process was valid. The voter fraud and election irregularities in this case are most disturbing, especially with the vote being so close. If the courts decide that some county did not have a legal election and orders a re-vote, so be it. Anything else would not be fair.<P>I myself have felt rushed and hurried during the voting, because there are usually a line of folks waiting impatiently behind me for their turn too. Sometimes seniors (and I bet you and I too at times) have too much pride to ask for help or don't want to seem helpless.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Floridaballot.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000051||Black88GT||11-11-2000||04:41 PM||||batboy, true that it says they must recount if the difference is less then 1%, which it is.  Where does it say they must recount TWICE?  Then the Democraps want to look at all of the 19,000 ballots who voted twice and determine the voters "intent".  I wonder who they think the voter intended to vote for.<P>Also, if the old people down there had trouble with seeing the ballot, why didn't they ask for help?  My friend had to help her grandfather, 90 years old, at the voting booth here in MD.  It was that simple.  Saying afterwards "I voted for the wrong guy" or whatever is a day late and a dollar short.<P>Those "voting irregularities" is just liberal media B.S. trying to sway public opinion for Gore.  None of those allegations have ANY concrete evidence.<P>I would also have to disagree with the statement about Bush keeping his mouth shut.  It is Gore and his campaign that is going crazy about the recounting and revoting (never happen).  Bush has only spoken publicly twice to my knowledge on this topic.  Gore had his nice little photoshoot football game with his picture perfect family (aww what a kodak moment).<P>Finally batboy, your saying that we should all wait until we count the absentee ballots.  I agree 100%.  However, shouldn't we not judge the popular vote until we get the absentee votes in?  Remember, many absentee voters are military, and we all know who they usually vote for... <P>("I said the majority of the American people want Gore for president, which is quite true, just look at the popular vote.")<P>IMHO of course<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
