Z||000064||batboy||11-12-2000||09:29 AM||||Cliff makes a good point. As mature adults, we ought to be able to discuss ANYTHING without resorting to personal attacts. I'm not picking on anyone because several of us are guilty of this, but clearly Fiero5 was making a personal attack. Doesn't matter if he was flamed before or not, you should be able to make good arguements without personally attacking someone else. Remember, two wrongs don't make a right.<P>Personally, I liked Saturday Night Live's Idea of making them both president and having a sitcom "Odd Couple" in the White House. Last night SNL was poking fun at both candidates and it was hillarious. At times they are both acting like little school kids.<P>I know that I added fuel to the fire in this topic, but I was merely exercising my right to free speech. You don't have to like what I said or support my opinion. If anyone feels like I was picking on them personally, I'm sorry. Email me personally and vent if you want. As long as you don't call me or my family any dirty names, I'll probably apologize in return. After the election is over (it ain't over yet}, life will go on. It's not the end of the world either way.||||reg||1
