Z||000067||Fiero5||11-12-2000||10:39 AM||||Wow, have you heard the latest on the news? There is now talk by some of looking into doing one of two things, if the recounts continue to be contraversial and problematic.<P>1) Throw out Florida alltogether as doing a revote is out of the question. That would be great, now "everyones" vote in Florida might not count. This would then conveniatly give Gore the win as he has the higher count right now. I can see the lawsuits grow out of that brilliant decision.<P>2) Waite till the end of all the recounts, and then use the popular vote to decide. The argumant being that it would at least put the person in the White House who the majority voted for. But is that legal either? Wouldn't that mean changing a law or two in the constitution?<P>It get's better and better every time I turn on the news :o) At least the fact about the confusing ballot that didn't line up is being mentioned everywhere now, so maybe that will help get it fixed so it hopefully won't happen again. They said that last year in Florida sixteen thousand votes were thrown out due to a similar problem. I guess they not only didn't learn, they made it worse.<BR>Ya gotta love it :o)||||reg||1
