Z||000071||Black88GT||11-12-2000||03:41 PM||||Someone correct me if I am wrong, but aren't the absentee ballots due in tomorrow? Or is it next Monday?  I can't remember.  <P>I hope they come in tomorrow, they should give Bush more breathing room then 327 votes.  <P>They are not going to have a revote OR throw out Florida's votes.  The most they can do is recount and recount and recount some more, which they probably will due until Gore comes out ahead.  There is no such thing as "revoting".  Voting is like dying in the English dictionary.  You can't "re-die".  Once its done, its done.<P>If I was Gore, I would not concede until the absentee ballots come in.  Some of the Republicans asking for him to concede are jumping the gun.  There is still a chance for Gore.  I would do the same thing if I ran a big election and came so close.  However, like I said before, most of the absentee ballots are from overseas servicemen and they usually go with Republicans (especially after the "glory days" of the Reagan Administration and the 8 years of hell with Clinton)<P><BR>IMHO<P>p.s. kelley if you have anything to say to me, email it.  No one else cares<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000072||deceler8||11-12-2000||05:07 PM||||The Florida recount is mandated by law, as the margin of victory was less than the 0.5% required in the Florida statute.<P>As far as I'm concerned, the recount is done (excepting the absentee ballots). Having computer ballots hand counted just introduces human error into the process as well as subjective interpretation of what a voter tried to vote for.<P>The votes (again, excepting absentee) have been counted twice and Mr. Bush has come out on top both times. It's time for both sides to tone down the rhetoric and wait for the absentees to be counted.<P>And whomever comes up with the lesser vote total should concede. No Mulligans allowed.||||reg||1
Z||000073||DJRice||11-13-2000||03:46 PM||||The real question here is Why are we still using these decade old punch cards?  I know full well that a secure voting system could be set up using computers that would save countless time and even give you the option to double check your vote before it gets submitted to the master voting system.    <P>Imagine it just for a second:<BR><B><I>YOU HAVE SELECTED PAT BUCHANAN FOR PRESIDENT.  ARE YOU SURE?</B></I><P>If I can log on to my computer, or anyone's computer for that matter, and discuss my car with over 1000 people all over the world...I sure should be able to vote on a PC with big buttons for each candiate and feel confident that my vote will get logged properly.<P>At least then, our problem would not be those people who "exeperienced difficulty" (is that PC enough) with the punch card ballots.  Our problem would be those 15 year old kids whose parents got them an E-machine with broadband internet service for christmas hacking into the system and adding pokemon to the ballot.<P><BR>BTW, I wonder how Buchanan feels to hear the media say a vote for him couldnt possibly have been done on purpose???<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
