Z||000076||mrfixit58||11-13-2000||05:34 PM||||HAHAHAHAHAHA!!!!! LMbuttO. No Offence!<P>Regarding the recount in Florida: As has been said before... it's the law. Bush won the first AND second recount. The reason Gore gained votes in the hand count is because he is only recounting them in largly DEMOCRATE rich counties, DUH. If the officials decide to extend the cut-off date from 5:00 pm Tuesday, then Bush needs to start counting the REPUBLICAN counties. <P>To be fair to both parties, let's just recount the ENTIRE 2,000,000+ votes for the ENTIRE state by hand. Be sure to shake each card so the paper dots fall out. Hold each one up to the light to see if it looks like someone TRIED to punch it. Never mind that it's only the jobless (a.k.a. retirees) that will be doing the re-counting (Excuse me sir while I put on my bi-focals). Yea, that's what we should do.... Computers always make errors that favor the Republican party. PU-LEASE!!!<P>The punch card method has been used for YEARS (and, yes, they DO line up if you puch the CORRECT arrow). No one, democrate OR republican, complained about the method when Reagan or Bush, Sr. was elected, nor did they complain about it when Clinton was elected. So, after eight years of a democrate in the oval office are we now more STUPID then the twelve years of republican presidency? Could the fact the the republicans have the majority vote in the House and Senate and that it's time to appoint a couple of Supreme Court Judges have something to do with all the fuss by the democrates?<P>Bush won... Gore didn't. I hate it when a football game ends on a controversial call, too. It sucks to be on the losing side but, life goes on. If changes need to be made, then let's make them... apply them to the next election. But for now, let's MOVE ON! <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||4
