Z||000081||Songman||11-14-2000||06:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by batboy:<BR><B>Is that before or after he was arrested for drunk driving? LOL</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think surely that must have been after he got a DUI 25 years ago... with no record of it since...<P>Come on... how many of you here ever had a DUI? I never have, but some of my friends have. Do we hold that against them? Even the next day or week or month, muchless 25 years later... And the exit polls showed that the strategically released DUI news had no effect on voters... Give me a break!<P>I had a Democrat from GA over the weekend tell me he hoped that drunk did win so he could run the country into the ground and teach Republicans a lesson.... again... Give me a break!<P>Partisan politics has gone too far. Do we have any other Americans here or am I the only one? Sure, I voted for Bush, but as my website says, for character not for party. As I said before, I am a registered Democrat but didn't see any character in the Democratic candidate.<P>Regardless of who you voted for, this has gotten out of hand. Not just on he forum, but all over the world. There are rules, there are laws, and there is a Constitution. If you want it changed, that s what you do. But for now, you go with it as is... no lawsuits or anything like that... just as it is. <P>||||reg||1
